Z||000018||AkursedX||07-29-2001||07:24 PM||||I think that the RX-7 is at least as good, if not better than a Fiero as far as being the best bang for the buck.  But as far as which one is better?  I think that comes down to personal preference.  I personally think the RX-7 is a better bang for the buck, especially if you know alot about rotaries.  But like I said, that's just my opinion.<P>Stock for stock, I would put an RX-7 turbo just about even with a 2.8 Fiero.  I think the 2.8 is a better made car, but I think the RX-7 has more potential for performance.  I really think it comes down to a personal preference and the availibility of the cars.  <P>When I was looking to buy a car, I was looking at Fieros, MR2's, RX-7's, older Supras, Talons, and Daytonas.  I probably looked at over 40 cars of varying conditions, and it just happened that my 88GT was the best car at the cheapest price, so that is what I went with.  And of course I fell in love with my Fiero, but I would of fallen in love with any other those cars, if I would of found one in the same condition at the same price.  <P>The RX-7 also has a bigger aftermarket that our Fieros, so that is another bonus for it.  But rotary turbos have a knack for blowing up alot earlier than a Fiero that was similarly maintained.  <BR>So if you don't know alot about rotaries, the Fiero would be more appealing and more cost efficient.  Plus finding a well maintained RX-7 at a good price is alot harder to find than a Fiero.  <P>Personally, I love the RX-7, and I still plan on owning one, along with my Fieros.  And there are alot of other imports I like as well.  If people want to hate imports, that is their choice, I could really care less. <P>As for my favorite musclecar?  I always liked anything with a hemi in it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">  Chargers, Cuda's, Roadrunners, etc. I love all Mopars!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
