Z||000035||JohnnyK||07-30-2001||01:52 PM||||Ok, let me rephrase, in the short to mid haul, the Japanese cars are worth a lot more. For instance, take my 1995 Honda Accord. Has barely gone down in value compared to American cars (Mind you, the Honda accord holds it's value exceptionally well)..<P>Anyways, I'd have to say, the 69 Mach 1 is a better looker than the Shelby..||||reg||1
Z||000036||Songman||07-30-2001||02:12 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AkursedX:<BR><B>I agree that the 427 Cobra is one hell of a car as well.  <BR>But wasn't the 289 cobra actually the won that won all of those races and really put Shelby's name on the map?  I remember hearing that somewhere.  I don't think the 427's were used for road racing. <BR>Correct me if I'm wrong</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>The AIF 289's were the racers. The 427's were heavy in the front and slow to build RPMs, but the torque was outrageous! Pure muscle...<P>But the 427s came first... <P><BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 07-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000037||b lo 0||07-30-2001||02:57 PM||||Songman's right-FIA 289's were primarily used for road racing, as they were better balanced.  Some 427's were used, 0-60 in about 4.5 secs, but didn't handle up to par with the Ferraris and COrvettes of the day.  That IS a 427, again Songman is right-289's were flat across the bottom of the grille, however, the FIA 289's (race versions) had flares, although different, sidepipes (smaller than the 427) and had cutback doors and "suitcase" dimples in the trunk lid (FIA rules required that a standardized "suitcase" size box fit in the trunk-also the only reason GT40's had trunks).  Damn sweet car, tho.  Wanted one since I was 5  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="1">'85 GT (in progress)<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">      <BR>White Lightnin!  (NOT moonshine, for all you hillbillies!)</FONT>||||reg||1
