Z||000040||Songman||07-30-2001||05:42 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by b lo 0:<BR><B>Songman's right-FIA 289's were primarily used for road racing...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Having a dyslexic moment... FIA, AIR, FAI... it was the race car! hehe<P>I test drove a kit car Cobra 427 one time. No a bad price at $26,000. Real 427 with a 4-speed. Two things that kept me from buying it. On this particular kit, my head was higher than the top of the windshield, and also, because of the transmission hump the pedals were moved way over to the left. actually had to sit at an angle in the car to drive it...<P>I do have a real 1964 427 CobraJet engine complete with 4-speed tranny. It came out of a 64 Galaxie convertible that my parents used to have. I always said that one day I'll build a Cobra for this.. Almost as close as you can come to the real thing...<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
